snippet.description:
I bought a Mini Hamstick from @GigaPartsHuntsville through Amazon.  I got it as a place holder on my ATAS mount.  My ATAS was too tall for me to get my truck in the garage.  So, when the ATAS is off, the Mini Hamstick is on.
I wasn't sure it would work well.  I figured it would allow me to monitor 20m while mobile, but had no idea I could make contacts with it.  That was until I hear @HamRadioAdventureGuy KE8PZN at a park.  I put out my call and James picked me right up.  
From that moment, I knew I needed to attempt a park activation with the tiny little stick.
